1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,320
That is Kirchhoff's first law, the junction law.

2
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:11,289
The algebraic sum of the currents at a junction is zero, counting currents in as positive and currents out as negative.

3
00:00:11,289 --> 00:00:16,093
Charge cannot pile up at a point, so it is really the conservation of charge.

